cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Datasheet: what laboratory automation control interfaces specify for authorization, audit and reconstructability"
message: "If you use this coding frame or dataset, please cite it."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Tran
    given-names: John D.
    name-suffix: PhD
    affiliation: Porcupine Labs
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-02
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  A coding frame and accumulating dataset recording what publicly published
  control interfaces for laboratory automation define for action-level
  authorization, command records, the distinction between a policy refusal and
  a mechanical failure, revocation in flight, identity binding, and record
  integrity. Published at draft stage so the instrument can be criticized
  before a population is coded against it.
keywords:
  - laboratory automation
  - AI safety
  - biosecurity
  - specification review
  - authorization
